lesson: 81
title: Equal groups
stars: 0
explain: When there are several groups and every group holds the same number, multiply to find how many in all.
explain: The number of groups times the number in each group gives the total.
explain: 4 bags with 6 apples in each bag hold 4 × 6 = 24 apples.
vars: a=name t=thing g=2..9 k=2..10
answer: g * k
exercise: {a} has {g} bags. Each bag holds {k} {t}. How many {t} does {a} have in all?
exercise: There are {g} boxes with {k} {t} in each box. How many {t} are there altogether?
exercise: {a} makes {g} piles of {t}. Each pile has {k} {t}. How many {t} are in the piles?
exercise: {g} children each have {k} {t}. How many {t} do the children have in all?
exercise: {a} fills {g} jars, putting {k} {t} in every jar. How many {t} did {a} put in the jars?
exercise: Each tray has {k} {t}. There are {g} trays. How many {t} are on the trays?
test: How many {t} are needed to put {k} {t} into each of {g} baskets?
test: {a} buys {g} packs of {t}, and every pack contains {k} {t}. What is the total number of {t}?
test: {k} {t} go into one bag. {a} fills {g} such bags. How many {t} is that?
test: There are {g} tables in the room, and {a} sets {k} {t} on each one. How many {t} did {a.he} set out?
exercise: {a} has {g} boxes of {t} with {k} {t} in every box. How many {t} are there in total?
exercise: How many {t} are there altogether in {g} bags of {k}?
exercise: {g} friends in Ohio each bring {k} {t} to a party. How many {t} do they bring combined?
exercise: There are {k} {t} per pack and {g} packs. How many {t} are there?
exercise: {a} gives {k} {t} apiece to {g} children. How many {t} does {a} give away in all?
exercise: A shop in London has {g} shelves, and every shelf holds {k} {t}. How many {t} are on the shelves altogether?
exercise: There are {g.words} plates with {k} {t} on each plate. How many {t} are on the plates?
exercise: {a} makes {g} gift bags for a party in New Zealand and puts {k} {t} in each one. How many {t} does {a} need?
test: Every one of the {g} tables in a café in Sydney has {k} {t} on it. How many {t} are on the tables in total?
test: How many {t} do {g} children hold if each of them holds {k}?
test: {a} bought {g} bags of {t} at a market in Toronto, {k} {t} per bag. How many {t} did {a} buy?
test: {k} {t} sit on each of the {g} trays. Find the number of {t} on all the trays.
test: In Ireland, {a} made {g} equal stacks of {t}, {k.words} in each stack. How many {t} are in the stacks combined?
test: A box of {t} holds {k}. How many {t} are in {g} such boxes?
exercise: {g} bags, {k} {t} each. how many {t} all up
exercise: {g} kids got {k} {t} each, how many {t} is that
exercise: {a} made {g+1} piles — no wait, {g} piles — {k} {t} in each. how many {t}
exercise: {g} boxes of {k} {t}, my mate counted {g*k+k}, nah one box too many. whats the real number
test: {k} {t} in every bag n {a} got {g} bags. total?
test: {g} plates, {k} {t} on each, oh n theres 3 forks too. how many {t}
test: {a} says {g} groups of {k} is {g*k-k}?? thats wrong innit, how many really
exam: Determine the aggregate quantity of {t} contained in {g.words} receptacles, each of which contains {k.words} {t}.
exam: It is given that {a} is in possession of {g} bags, each holding {k} {t}. Ascertain the total number of {t} so held.
exam: Compute the product of {g} and {k}.
exam: State the total number of {t} distributed, given that each of {g} pupils received precisely {k} {t}.
exercise: When Grandpa passed away, he left each of his {g} grandchildren {k} dollars. How many dollars did he leave them in all?
exercise: Since Dad was let go, he has done odd jobs for {g} weeks, {k} hours each week. How many hours of odd jobs has he done?
test: {a} says each of the {g} bags has {k+1} {t}. porkies — it's {k} a bag, i counted. so how many {t} altogether, smartarse
